          <div class="msv__step-num">05</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Assemble Your Financial Documentation</h3>
            <p>Prepare 6 months of bank statements, SSA benefit letters, pension award letters, tax returns (Form 1040), brokerage statements, and any other proof of income. Have certified Spanish translations prepared for all key documents.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">06</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Complete Form EX-01</h3>
            <p>Download and complete Spain's national long-stay visa application form (EX-01). Complete in Spanish or with certified translation. Two originals are required. Sign and date close to your appointment date.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">07</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Attend In-Person Appointment in Coral Gables</h3>
            <p>Appear in person at the Consulate General of Spain, 2655 Le Jeune Rd, Suite 203, Coral Gables, FL 33134. Bring all originals and copies. Pay the visa fee (approximately €80–€100 per applicant, typically by money order). Biometrics may be collected.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">08</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Wait for Decision &amp; Travel to Spain</h3>
            <p>Processing takes 10–16 weeks. Collect your visa on approval. Travel to Spain within the visa's validity window and register with the local Foreigners' Office (Oficina de Extranjeros) within 30 days of arrival.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

